{
  "manufacturer": "Hitachi",
  "manufacturer_slug": "hitachi",
  "model": "WJ-C1 series inverter (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "wj-c1",
  "short_model": "Hitachi WJ-C1",
  "aliases": [
    "WJ-C1",
    "WJ-C1 series"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Hitachi WJ-C1 inverters using the built-in RS485 port in Modbus-RTU mode; User's Guide NT361X, chapters 11 and 18.",
  "summary": "The WJ-C1 compact inverter has an RS485 port that speaks Modbus RTU. Coils give run/stop, direction, reset and the intelligent input and output signals; holding registers give status words, the frequency command, all d-group monitors, trip history and every parameter. This map covers control, the main monitors, the latest trip record and the communication parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The manual prints coil and register numbers in hex starting at 0001h and says the start number in the frame is the register number minus 1 (its coil read example asks for coil 0007h with 0006h). So wire address = printed number - 1: register 1001h is wire 0x1000."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "WJ-C1 Series Inverter User's Guide",
    "doc_number": "NT361X",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.hitachi-iesa.com/sites/default/files/supportingdocs/WJ-C1_UsersGuide_NT361X.pdf",
    "pages": "ch. 11 (RS485 communication, endian selection p. 11-2-14), ch. 18 pp. 18-1-1 to 18-2-4 (coils, special registers, d group, F group), A and C groups"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Two-register values are printed as (High) then (Low) register. With Endian selection [P400] = 00 Big endian (default) a two-register value 01020304h is sent as 01 02 03 04, which is ABCD. Little endian (01) and special endian (02) change the byte order; trip history registers 0012h-004Eh always read big endian.",
    "Only a working subset is listed: control coils, status words, main d-group monitors, trip monitor 1, F001-F004, A001/A002 and the C07x communication settings. Trip monitors 2-6 follow at 001Ch, 0026h, 0030h, 003Ah and 0044h with the same layout as trip monitor 1. The full parameter list is in chapter 18.",
    "Accumulated input power [d015] is in units of 1 kWh multiplied by the [b079] gain, so no fixed unit is given here.",
    "Inverter state A (0003h) has no code 1 in the source.",
    "Coils 0010h-0058h can also be read as packed words at 1E01h-1E05h, and coils 0001h-000Fh written via 1F01h; not listed separately.",
    "The rotation direction monitor [d003] is printed with keypad symbols only (F / o / r for 0-2); the exact code-to-symbol order is not stated, so no value list is given."
  ],
